  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final text sets 24-hour regulator reporting and 72-hour customer notice for confirmed incidents, covering incidents regardless of known cause. S2 keeps the 5% limit and per-model rates for customers, but has no automatic sales stop and an open-ended, regulator-discretionary remediation period, which is the main weakening. S3 gives a 6-year retrofit window (Northwind-favourable) and S5 keeps an 8/100k mandatory recall with no interim period, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k)."
